    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the lineup, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 81.21 efficiency score. His matchup against Rocker is highly favorable due to a strong platoon advantage and his prime leadoff spot, which maximizes his exposure to run-scoring opportunities. **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** also carry high expectations; both benefit from a target-rich environment against Eduardo Rodriguez. **Pages**, in particular, sees a slight boost from a favorable park factor and the opposing starter\u2019s slow delivery, which keeps our stolen base aggressive strategy in play. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Jackson Merrill** all register scores well into the 60s and 70s, as they capitalize on softer matchups against Holmes and Cristian Javier, where high-efficiency platoon splits and favorable park dimensions align to boost their scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's board involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 45.68 score. While his potential is clear, the optimizer favored the more consistent efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** and the platoon-adjusted volume of our outfielders. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the bench at 41.74; despite his elite tools, his poor historical BvP and a disadvantageous matchup against Jones made him a liability compared to the higher-floor options currently starting. Managers should keep a close watch on **Liam Hicks** and **Jackson Merrill**, as their scores are contingent on pending lineup confirmations; if either is dropped in the batting order, their efficiency ratings will undergo an immediate downward revision. Lastly, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a tough arm in Luzardo, his base projection remains high enough to warrant a start despite the SP skill penalty, serving as the anchor for our infield production today.",
